Description: Fits TVSurvBART, a continuous-time Bayesian survival model for
    longitudinal data recorded in counting-process (start-stop) form. The
    hazard combines a baseline hazard (natural cubic spline or piecewise
    constant), a Bayesian additive regression tree ensemble of the
    time-varying covariates, and subject-level random effects (a random
    intercept, optionally with a random slope in time) with a Huang-Wand
    covariance prior. Posterior inference is by Markov chain Monte Carlo; the
    prediction functions return posterior draws of the cumulative hazard for
    training and new subjects.
